WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.980
Out-of-order speculative execution for LLM agents cuts latency on long-tool calls while keeping correctness intact. This is Models &amp; Agents, episode 190. Tomasu LLM runs future agent actions in isolated sandboxes, and commits results only after validation against committed state. The runtime improves performance on three benchmarks that spans sub-second to minutes long-tool calls. It reaches 1.31 times on one

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:37.960
100 sweet bench verified tasks. It reaches 1.35 times on 28 terminal bench 2.0 tasks.

00:00:38.540 --> 00:00:44.360
It reaches 1.27 times matched progress on 18 sweet marathon sessions.

00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:49.960
4,010 audited commit validation records show zero false accepts.

00:00:50.660 --> 00:00:56.060
The approach targets idle time created by compilers, test suites, and repository commands.

00:00:56.060 --> 00:01:03.780
In Model Updates, Frontier LLMs reached censored mean absolute error within 10% of state-of-the-art

00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:08.700
random survival forests on several cancer types in the MSK-chored cohort.

00:01:09.580 --> 00:01:16.620
GPT 5.6-sol posts lower error than the random survival forest baseline for prostate cancer

00:01:16.620 --> 00:01:17.440
in that cohort.

00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:23.500
Feature ablations indicate the models prioritize clinical variables similarly to specialized

00:01:23.500 --> 00:01:24.700
survival models.

00:01:24.700 --> 00:01:30.960
Accuracy remains inconsistent across cancer types and institutions, and concordance index

00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:33.640
scores stay lower than the specialized baselines.

00:01:34.640 --> 00:01:41.860
Across 17 instruction tuned models ranging from 1.5 billion to 72 billion parameters, persona

00:01:41.860 --> 00:01:45.620
and formatting instructions restructure intermediate representations.

00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:51.080
Safety instructions produce changes statistically indistinguishable from a minimal baseline.

00:01:51.080 --> 00:01:56.220
line. Restrictive and explicitly permissive safety instructions engage near-identical

00:01:56.220 --> 00:02:02.340
computational pathways, with mean-centered kernel alignment correlation of 0.997.

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:08.640
Safety penetration remains below 10% even at 70 billion to 72 billion scale.

00:02:09.850 --> 00:02:15.320
Representational depth predicts behavioral effect size with spearman row of 0.761.

00:02:15.320 --> 00:02:21.680
Split conformal claim filtering applied to multi-hop retrieval augmented generation raises

00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:30.160
the fraction of fully supported retained claims to between 95.80 and 97.20% at the 95%

00:02:30.160 --> 00:02:41.340
target. Only 4.41 to 31.09% of generated claims are retained at that target. 9.70 to 51.40%

00:02:41.340 --> 00:02:50.540
of responses remain non-empty. The evaluation covers LOMA 3.18B and GPT-40 mini. Changing terminology

00:02:50.540 --> 00:02:57.460
alone reverses which side of an issue a model supports in 16.9% of matched comparisons across

00:02:57.460 --> 00:03:04.200
seven open-weight models and 10 contentious topics. Stated political ideology systematically shifts

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:12.280
responses toward the user's position. 12 LLMs achieve 95.6% mean appropriateness on honesty,

00:03:12.820 --> 00:03:19.160
autonomy, and confidentiality scenarios across medicine, law, finance, and national security.

00:03:19.780 --> 00:03:27.500
Correct domain-specific justification use varies from 25.6% to 76.9% across models.

00:03:27.500 --> 00:03:33.760
Varying stakes reveal severe but localized failures where models alter responses even though

00:03:33.760 --> 00:03:36.740
the underlying professional obligation remains unchanged.

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:43.060
Evoke supplies goal diversity at fixed states during post-training to elicit pre-trained

00:03:43.060 --> 00:03:45.740
world knowledge without additional world model training.

00:03:46.140 --> 00:03:52.240
It reports improved task performance, unseen environment generalization, and data efficiency

00:03:52.240 --> 00:03:54.740
across diverse tasks in three backbones.

00:03:54.740 --> 00:04:01.560
The heterogeneity-driven team selection framework profiles individual capability plus decorrelation

00:04:01.560 --> 00:04:04.500
in error patterns and divergence in predictive behavior.

00:04:05.100 --> 00:04:10.560
It applies an efficient greedy search to select a small team from a candidate pool and consistently

00:04:10.560 --> 00:04:12.760
outperforms quality-only baselines.

00:04:13.560 --> 00:04:19.440
D-Edit adds iterative token-to-token editing to a diffusion-based drafter, so later predictions

00:04:19.440 --> 00:04:22.840
can repair earlier errors using bidirectional context.

00:04:22.840 --> 00:04:32.960
On QN34B and QN38B, it reaches macro average speed-ups of 5.72 times and 5.97 times over

00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:35.760
auto-regressive generation under greedy decoding.

00:04:36.620 --> 00:04:41.900
Anchor label relabeling replaces corpus labels with distributions from greedy target rollouts.

00:04:42.360 --> 00:04:48.140
In rollout anchors places draft blocks inside target rollouts to expose the drafter to target

00:04:48.140 --> 00:04:50.920
generated context at no extra target cost.

00:04:50.920 --> 00:04:58.400
The framework increases greedy accepted length by up to 36.5% over D-flash on fixed vision

00:04:58.400 --> 00:05:00.020
language and text corpora.

00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:05.360
Nina Zander connects layers of frozen models from different families with a single train

00:05:05.360 --> 00:05:06.660
shared latent adapter.

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:12.520
The configuration combining the first five layers of Pythia, with the remaining 27 layers

00:05:12.520 --> 00:05:20.380
of RWKV, reduces transformer key value cache by 84.4%, with accuracy not significantly

00:05:20.380 --> 00:05:22.440
differently from RWKV alone.

00:05:23.340 --> 00:05:27.760
No composed model matched parent model Pythia on multiple choice accuracy.

00:05:28.640 --> 00:05:33.420
Doct 2-Lora generates a Lora adapter for each paper, so every point in the embedding

00:05:33.420 --> 00:05:37.860
space corresponds to an LLM that can be queried in natural language.

00:05:38.480 --> 00:05:43.780
On American Physical Society papers, the average of subfield instruction produces labels closer

00:05:43.780 --> 00:05:45.820
to official names than five baselines.

00:05:45.820 --> 00:05:51.280
A small, invertible transform makes the embedding's competitive for search while remaining

00:05:51.280 --> 00:05:53.260
mappable back to an LLM.

00:05:53.720 --> 00:06:00.300
A multi-domain benchmark of approximately 9.2000 instances tests narrative-infilling across

00:06:00.300 --> 00:06:05.480
encyclopedic text, common-sense stories, news articles, and visual narratives.

00:06:06.160 --> 00:06:12.900
Gemma 22B achieves the highest qualitative score of 4.02 out of 5, outperforming models

00:06:12.900 --> 00:06:14.340
over 10 times larger.

00:06:14.340 --> 00:06:20.540
Explicit chain of thought reasoning yields only a 0.6% marginal improvement.

00:06:21.180 --> 00:06:27.780
Clinique bench contains 333 clinician-authored tasks, each with a virtual patient, clinical

00:06:27.780 --> 00:06:30.880
tools, and task-specific success criteria.

00:06:31.500 --> 00:06:35.420
More than 35 clinicians contributed to case-authoring and evaluation.

00:06:36.340 --> 00:06:42.060
Best performing models succeed on less than 30% of tasks, even though diagnosis accuracy

00:06:42.060 --> 00:06:48.880
reaches 90.7%. Speculative decoding lets a small drafter propose tokens that a larger

00:06:48.880 --> 00:06:55.140
target verifies in parallel. The quality gain disappears above roughly 70 billion parameters,

00:06:55.500 --> 00:07:00.080
because the drafter's error rate begins to offset the parallel verification benefit.

00:07:00.720 --> 00:07:06.880
A single early mismatch forces the entire block to be discarded. Adding iterative editing passes

00:07:06.880 --> 00:07:12.960
lets later predictions supply bidirectional context that repairs earlier errors without restarting

00:07:12.960 --> 00:07:18.500
the draft. This raises accepted length but adds a second forward pass per editing round,

00:07:18.940 --> 00:07:26.080
trading roughly 200 milliseconds of latency for the observed 5.7 times speed up on Q334b.

00:07:26.660 --> 00:07:32.480
Use plain speculative decoding when the drafter matches the target family and context length stays

00:07:32.480 --> 00:07:38.760
under 8,000 tokens. Switch to editing or anchor relabeling once the drafter is drawn from a different

00:07:38.760 --> 00:07:46.220
family or the corpus contains many long toolcalls. Try Tamasu LLM on SWE bench verified tasks

00:07:46.220 --> 00:07:53.780
to measure the 1.31 times latency reduction on long running toolcalls. Run context-adap scenarios

00:07:53.780 --> 00:08:01.600
on any of the 12 evaluated models to check domain-specific justification rates. Test evoke post-training on

00:08:01.600 --> 00:08:07.000
a held-out environment to observe gains in unseen generalization without extra-world

00:08:07.000 --> 00:08:07.860
model training.

00:08:08.480 --> 00:08:14.380
Apply doc to Lora embeddings to a set of APS papers and query the resulting Lora adapters

00:08:14.380 --> 00:08:15.780
for sub-field descriptions.

00:08:16.540 --> 00:08:22.240
Additional results from the Hallou Scoring 2026 shared task on Arabic hallucination detection

00:08:22.240 --> 00:08:24.280
are expected in the coming weeks.

00:08:24.960 --> 00:08:30.020
Further scaling experiments on NAMO's sparse attention are anticipated from the same research

00:08:30.020 --> 00:08:30.400
group.

00:08:31.120 --> 00:08:37.340
Expanded Clinique Bench Tasks covering additional clinical specialties are under development by the authoring clinicians.

00:08:37.800 --> 00:08:45.300
Before we go, watch for new numbers on long horizon agent reliability from the next round of terminal bench evaluations.

